WEBVTT

00:04.500 --> 00:06.870
Man, this stress is gonna make me go bald.

00:08.400 --> 00:11.860
But the nobles agreed to offer you a loan.

00:11.860 --> 00:15.290
That's what's stressing me out.

00:15.290 --> 00:19.590
They'll keep telling me what to do, 
so I can't run things how I want.

00:20.250 --> 00:22.930
The priests of Vienna's cult say her mercy

00:22.930 --> 00:26.370
spreads throughout the 
heavens and fills the earth.

00:26.370 --> 00:31.480
If that's true, then why are there 
still people suffering in poverty?

00:31.480 --> 00:36.940
The age of Vienna's cult and the Rhodesian
 Empire in its thrall is coming to an end.

00:36.940 --> 00:40.270
It is not some goddess
 who will save us. It is man.

00:40.270 --> 00:43.850
The teachings of the great Solomon,

00:43.850 --> 00:47.630
who ruled over the Demon Kings and 
commanded monsters, are our only salvation.

00:48.710 --> 00:49.980
Solomon!

00:50.560 --> 00:53.470
These are talismans of the great Solomon.

00:50.860 --> 00:53.190
Down with the nobles!

00:53.190 --> 00:54.390
Solomon!

00:53.470 --> 00:57.420
I'm offering them at the 
low price of twenty copper coins.

00:57.420 --> 00:58.450
I'll take one!

00:57.960 --> 00:59.060
What's going on?

00:58.450 --> 01:00.550
I want one, too!

00:59.060 --> 01:02.350
Those seals don't look magical at all.

01:02.860 --> 01:04.860
It's a religious scam.

01:06.620 --> 01:09.200
How dare you disrupt 
public order, lawbreaker!

01:09.200 --> 01:10.960
Arrest them!

01:11.820 --> 01:14.890
I have no cure for fools.

01:20.130 --> 01:22.090
I can't breathe...

01:22.090 --> 01:25.320
It was folly to defy the great Solomon.

01:25.930 --> 01:28.490
Okay, haven't you gone far enough?

01:28.490 --> 01:30.180
Wh-What?

01:30.460 --> 01:31.430
Byaku!

01:44.900 --> 01:47.160
Hey, are you all right, Saintess?

01:47.160 --> 01:48.880
Byaku, you idiot!

01:48.880 --> 01:51.410
You're supposed to keep people 
like that way from me!

01:52.970 --> 01:54.930
Either way, we're getting out of here.

01:54.930 --> 01:58.250
I'm not fighting two former S-rankers.

02:05.110 --> 02:07.450
That was teleportation magic!

02:07.450 --> 02:11.330
Only a handful of mages can 
cast such high-level spells.

02:12.170 --> 02:14.190
Just who were they...

02:26.140 --> 02:34.690
<b>My Daughter Left the Nest and Returned an S-Rank Adventurer</b>

03:46.740 --> 03:52.160
<b>Episode 5 "The Road to Bordeaux"</b>

03:56.030 --> 03:57.330
Welcome!

04:02.640 --> 04:05.450
The spring festival is so much fun.

04:05.450 --> 04:06.040
Yeah.

04:06.350 --> 04:08.550
Are you two enjoying yourselves?

04:08.840 --> 04:10.190
Yes.

04:10.630 --> 04:13.560
You still can't get that off?

04:16.870 --> 04:20.570
I'm sorry, okay?
Could you let go of me already?

04:22.010 --> 04:24.460
No! I still don't forgive you!

04:25.460 --> 04:28.960
Wow, Bel. That's one huge baby.

04:28.960 --> 04:29.960
Chief.

04:29.960 --> 04:35.370
Everyone's finally agreed that we 
can fix up the road to Bordeaux.

04:36.290 --> 04:37.780
That's great news.

04:38.760 --> 04:42.520
Now we can triumphantly 
respond to the countess.

04:42.520 --> 04:43.630
Speaking of, Bel,

04:43.900 --> 04:46.870
I'd like you to deliver this to her.

04:47.890 --> 04:49.170
Me?

04:49.170 --> 04:54.320
You're skilled, but most importantly, 
Countess Bordeaux trusts you.

04:54.320 --> 04:56.430
I see. Very well.

04:57.050 --> 04:58.040
Thanks.

04:58.040 --> 04:59.270
When are you going?

04:59.270 --> 05:01.240
Soon would be best.

05:01.240 --> 05:06.100
In that case, you should come with us
 when we go to Orphen, Dad!

05:06.700 --> 05:08.580
Then that's what I'll do.

05:08.580 --> 05:10.570
I'll have you girls protect me.

05:11.530 --> 05:13.800
All right! When shall we depart?

05:13.800 --> 05:15.380
I could do tomorrow.

05:15.380 --> 05:17.950
But don't you want to say 
in Turnera a little longer?

05:17.950 --> 05:21.570
I'd much rather go on a journey with you!

05:22.570 --> 05:23.580
Hey!

05:23.810 --> 05:27.080
Tomorrow we're heading back 
to Orphen with my dad!

05:27.380 --> 05:30.350
What? Mr. Bel, you're 
coming out of retirement?

05:30.670 --> 05:34.110
No, not at all. I'm running an 
errand for the village chief.

05:34.340 --> 05:37.020
I see. That's too bad.

05:37.020 --> 05:40.350
Now that it's decided, 
let's head home and prepare!

05:50.110 --> 05:54.040
I'm going out. Be good while I'm gone.

05:54.550 --> 05:55.790
Now then...

05:55.790 --> 05:58.050
Dad, are you all ready?

05:58.050 --> 06:01.540
Yeah, let's be off. 
Look after the place while I'm gone.

06:01.810 --> 06:04.410
Sure thing. Go enjoy yourself.

06:04.410 --> 06:06.060
Bring back souvenirs.

06:06.350 --> 06:09.050
I'm not going there to have fun.

06:42.430 --> 06:45.720
We'll be in Bordeaux soon. 
I hope the sky doesn't open.

06:53.620 --> 06:58.900
I'm glad we made it, but would it be 
rude to show up soaked like this?

06:58.900 --> 07:00.840
We can visit tomorrow.

07:06.070 --> 07:10.210
They only had open seats at the counter.
 Business must be booming.

07:06.400 --> 07:08.390
What should I get?

07:08.390 --> 07:11.280
Everything looks so good. What about this?

07:10.210 --> 07:13.960
I'm hungry. What do you want, Dad?

07:11.280 --> 07:13.280
Sounds good. Let's get some of this.

07:13.280 --> 07:13.960
You want that?

07:13.960 --> 07:15.210
It'll be great! I promise!

07:15.210 --> 07:16.560
Should we order some, then?

07:16.560 --> 07:17.220
Yeah!

07:16.930 --> 07:20.590
Say, could I get some ale and anchovies?

07:21.700 --> 07:23.660
Huh? What?

07:26.610 --> 07:28.540
Wh-What is this?

07:28.540 --> 07:31.420
You put them on the bread, like this.

07:41.810 --> 07:44.670
Those aren't for beginners, Dad!

07:44.670 --> 07:47.820
They're super salty and have a unique smell.

07:49.100 --> 07:52.060
You should've warned me beforehand.

07:52.500 --> 07:56.780
I'm sorry. Some people like them,
 so I thought you might.

07:56.780 --> 07:59.170
You don't appreciate 
the appeal of anchovies?

07:59.450 --> 08:01.170
Listen here, Byaku.

08:01.170 --> 08:07.020
Anyone who calls them salty or smelly
might as well be saying what a hick they are.

08:07.690 --> 08:12.160
Whatever. You're only used to them
 because you're from Lucrecia.

08:12.160 --> 08:14.330
That stuff is gross.

08:14.720 --> 08:16.330
<i>Lucrecia, huh?</i>

08:16.330 --> 08:19.220
<i>They're so young, yet so far from home.</i>

08:20.570 --> 08:21.840
<i>Vestments?</i>

08:22.650 --> 08:27.490
<i>Come to think of it, the head temple 
of the cult of Vienna is in Lucrecia.</i>

08:27.740 --> 08:33.490
Gracious. What am I even doing 
out here in the middle of nowhere?

08:33.490 --> 08:35.950
Shut up. You talk too much.

08:37.030 --> 08:40.950
That's enough, Byaku! How dare you speak to your master that way?!

08:45.930 --> 08:48.110
Th-Thank...

08:49.810 --> 08:52.100
M-Mind your own business!

08:52.330 --> 08:53.100
Huh?

08:53.100 --> 08:55.410
Nobody asked for your help!

08:56.890 --> 08:59.060
Let go! Unhand me at—

08:59.060 --> 09:01.620
Forgive her for being so unsociable.

09:01.620 --> 09:04.520
Sorry for the trouble. Let's go, Saintess.

09:06.040 --> 09:08.240
Someone you know?

09:08.240 --> 09:09.400
No.

09:09.400 --> 09:11.110
What was that?!

09:11.690 --> 09:14.050
Just who do you think you are?!

09:14.050 --> 09:16.520
I'm the great Gort the Thunderbolt!

09:16.520 --> 09:19.460
All I see is a big fish 
in a small pond acting up.

09:19.460 --> 09:21.800
I've met plenty of guys like you.

09:22.110 --> 09:23.650
Screw you!

09:23.650 --> 09:25.630
I won't go easy 'cause you're a woman!

09:29.580 --> 09:32.260
You'll die young if you go picking fights

09:32.260 --> 09:35.200
when you can't gauge your opponents,
 Mr. Thunderbolt.

09:35.980 --> 09:37.080
You heard her!

09:37.770 --> 09:39.540
Get him, girlie!

09:38.380 --> 09:41.890
Guys like him give adventurers a bad name.

09:42.680 --> 09:45.390
So a swordsman lost to Anessa the archer?

09:45.820 --> 09:47.560
Do people really call him by that title?

09:48.600 --> 09:50.340
Obviously not.

09:51.020 --> 09:54.290
He's C-ranker who gave himself that nickname.

09:55.610 --> 09:57.080
Lame.

09:57.610 --> 09:59.390
Angeline, you of all people—

09:59.390 --> 10:01.600
Boy, that was satisfying!

10:02.330 --> 10:05.940
You laid Gort's annoying hide
 out with one blow!

10:05.940 --> 10:08.450
You must be a pretty strong adventurer.

10:08.450 --> 10:09.440
What's your rank?

10:09.440 --> 10:11.230
She and I are Triple A.

10:11.230 --> 10:11.810
Heck yeah!

10:11.810 --> 10:14.610
And the girl with the
 black hair over there is S.

10:15.540 --> 10:17.550
What? She's rank S?

10:17.550 --> 10:21.340
Wait, don't tell me you're
 the Black-Haired Valkyrie.

10:21.340 --> 10:23.310
What? The Demon King slayer?

10:24.520 --> 10:25.860
I suppose.

10:25.860 --> 10:27.350
Let me treat you!

10:27.350 --> 10:28.430
Me too, me too!

10:29.900 --> 10:32.260
I can't eat all of this.

10:32.260 --> 10:34.060
Neither can your old man.

10:34.060 --> 10:36.060
What? You're her dad?

10:37.130 --> 10:38.580
That red hair...

10:38.580 --> 10:40.570
The peg leg...

10:40.570 --> 10:44.750
Are you Belgrieve the Red Ogre?

10:46.320 --> 10:48.910
Yes! My dad is Belgrieve the Red—

10:49.810 --> 10:51.290
A-Ange.

10:51.680 --> 10:53.290
Sorry...

10:54.580 --> 10:56.350
I knew it!

10:56.350 --> 11:00.080
I flew right over when I heard 
rumors that you were here.

11:00.080 --> 11:03.430
I would've come to meet you
 if you'd told me you were coming.

11:03.430 --> 11:07.760
We were filthy and wet from the rain,
so we decided to visit tomorrow.

11:08.100 --> 11:10.470
The Bordeaux family owes you a great deal.

11:10.470 --> 11:14.280
We don't mind if you're wet or filthy.

11:15.690 --> 11:17.080
What should we do?

11:17.080 --> 11:19.770
If they're inviting us over, then why not?

11:19.770 --> 11:21.950
We get to sleep at a mansion, right?

11:21.950 --> 11:24.030
I bet their beds are fluffy!

11:24.610 --> 11:25.830
What say you, Dad?

11:26.800 --> 11:30.190
Well, I am here to deliver a letter.

11:30.190 --> 11:33.300
Now that we've been invited, 
we have no reason to decline.

11:34.250 --> 11:36.670
In that case, come with me, everyone.

11:40.830 --> 11:42.520
It's really coming down.

11:44.840 --> 11:47.300
I feel so funny in flowy clothes.

11:49.230 --> 11:51.080
You're just not used to it.

11:51.080 --> 11:52.570
It looks great on you.

11:52.570 --> 11:55.480
Really? In that case, I'm okay with it!

11:55.480 --> 11:57.150
I'm so glad you all made it.

11:57.880 --> 12:00.250
Hey, Seren. Have you been well?

12:00.250 --> 12:03.340
I have. You're looking well too, Ms. Angeline,

12:03.340 --> 12:06.820
Thank you for coming all the way here.

12:07.090 --> 12:10.020
We're sorry to impose
in the middle of the night.

12:10.020 --> 12:13.060
My sister is waiting for you. 
I'll show you to her.

12:13.450 --> 12:14.330
Thank you.

12:15.360 --> 12:16.630
I'm going with you.

12:17.700 --> 12:22.640
Helvetica is the one who 
tried to drag you off.

12:23.030 --> 12:26.010
We're just going to talk about the road.

12:26.010 --> 12:28.380
I'm going with you.

12:32.380 --> 12:33.790
Pardon us.

12:34.860 --> 12:36.770
Mr. Belgrieve!

12:40.150 --> 12:42.180
Thank you for coming.

12:42.180 --> 12:45.690
Your gallant figure is 
certainly a sight for sore eyes.

12:45.690 --> 12:48.740
I'm honored, Countess. 
It's good to see you, too.

12:48.740 --> 12:50.420
This is my daughter, Angeline.

12:50.640 --> 12:53.180
So you're Ms. Angeline!

12:53.180 --> 12:57.410
I cannot thank you enough 
for rescuing Seren.

12:57.850 --> 13:02.350
Are you the woman who 
wants to be my mother?

13:02.940 --> 13:04.670
H-Hey, Ange...

13:04.960 --> 13:07.050
Stay out of this, Dad.

13:07.050 --> 13:11.160
I'll never forgive you for trying to
 steal my dad while I was gone.

13:11.160 --> 13:15.070
But it <i>would</i> be for the best 
if he had someone nice around...

13:15.340 --> 13:18.140
My! Ms. Angeline, does this mean

13:18.140 --> 13:22.870
you might accept a relationship 
between me and Mr. Belgrieve?

13:23.190 --> 13:28.490
You've lost your mind if you think I'll hand 
him over to someone who tried to cart him off.

13:28.490 --> 13:32.230
Don't think you can become 
my mom that easily!

13:33.110 --> 13:35.380
How dare the likes of you speak to her so?!

13:35.840 --> 13:38.260
Silence, Ash.

13:39.150 --> 13:40.490
B-But...

13:40.490 --> 13:43.310
You would defy me?

13:44.090 --> 13:46.760
Forgive me.

13:47.020 --> 13:49.370
You're being rude, too.

13:49.370 --> 13:52.890
I won't be having any such
relationship with Lady Helvetica.

13:53.370 --> 13:55.770
Enough of this, Sister.

13:55.770 --> 13:58.700
You told me you'd already given up on this.

13:58.700 --> 14:02.000
But, Seren...

14:02.000 --> 14:03.530
P-Pardon me.

14:03.770 --> 14:06.240
Might we proceed with 
the business at hand?

14:07.720 --> 14:09.280
Forgive me.

14:09.940 --> 14:12.280
I've read the letter.

14:12.280 --> 14:16.500
I'm delighted to have your cooperation.

14:16.500 --> 14:22.160
Thank you. In that case, we'd like you 
to advise us on the specifics of your plan.

14:22.360 --> 14:26.650
Of course. Could I ask you
 to give me some time?

14:26.650 --> 14:30.170
Something of a troublesome
 problem has arisen, you see.

14:31.850 --> 14:37.060
Rodina

14:31.850 --> 14:37.060
Bordeaux

14:31.850 --> 14:37.060
Hazel

14:32.340 --> 14:36.950
West of Bordeaux, there is 
a small town called Hazel.

14:37.310 --> 14:39.560
Count Malta, who rules the area,

14:39.560 --> 14:43.790
has raised objections 
to sending laborers elsewhere

14:43.790 --> 14:47.910
when he's in the middle
of repairing his own roads.

14:48.350 --> 14:51.410
That sounds reasonable to me.

14:51.410 --> 14:56.250
But the construction in Hazel 
is already 90 percent complete.

14:56.250 --> 15:02.310
And we previously agreed that sending workers
on to the next project would be no issue.

15:04.390 --> 15:06.560
In other words, he's doing this on purpose.

15:06.710 --> 15:16.810
Hazel

15:06.710 --> 15:16.810
Bordeaux

15:06.710 --> 15:16.810
Orphen

15:06.710 --> 15:16.810
Estogal City

15:07.270 --> 15:12.960
Count Malta was relegated to 
Bordeaux from Estogal's capital city.

15:13.390 --> 15:16.360
He apparently lost a struggle for power.

15:17.030 --> 15:19.910
Because of this, he scorns Bordeaux

15:19.910 --> 15:23.320
as a backwater county
and finds fault in all we do.

15:24.810 --> 15:29.260
His behavior has escalated 
since our father's passing.

15:29.260 --> 15:31.570
I'm simply not a strong enough leader.

15:31.570 --> 15:35.500
Most influential figures are
 allied with the Bordeaux family,

15:35.960 --> 15:41.300
but some nobles are unhappy 
that my sister has taken over.

15:42.240 --> 15:49.590
We suspect Count Malta is egging them on,
but we have no concrete proof.

15:49.590 --> 15:52.790
Sounds like a complicated situation.

15:52.790 --> 15:59.590
But I'm not sure you should be 
discussing it with outsiders like us.

16:00.620 --> 16:02.540
I'm terribly sorry.

16:03.720 --> 16:05.720
There you are!

16:06.070 --> 16:09.610
Lady Sasha, you are a noble.
Please try to act like one.

16:09.610 --> 16:11.100
Oh, I know!

16:11.500 --> 16:14.080
This man here is Ashcroft.

16:14.080 --> 16:18.080
He's may be young, 
but he serves the Bordeaux family.

16:18.080 --> 16:21.240
He's inexperienced, 
but he's also a swordsman.

16:21.530 --> 16:24.250
Would you be willing to instruct him as well?

16:24.510 --> 16:29.090
Kindly refrain. I have no need for training.

16:29.930 --> 16:31.750
Honestly, you're so stubborn.

16:32.010 --> 16:36.760
Sasha, could you please entertain 
Ms. Angeline and Mr. Belgrieve?

16:37.010 --> 16:38.750
Yes, of course.

16:38.750 --> 16:43.080
Now then, if you don't mind 
waiting a bit for my reply,

16:43.080 --> 16:46.510
please make yourselves at home until then.

16:51.330 --> 16:55.030
I'm thinking about throwing a 
small party. What do you think?

16:55.030 --> 16:58.500
Good idea. I'll invite Ane and Miri, too.

16:58.500 --> 16:59.840
What about you, Dad?

16:59.840 --> 17:02.780
I might rest a bit.

17:03.500 --> 17:06.660
But I wanted to talk to you, too.

17:07.160 --> 17:11.500
I'm sorry. Ange, don't stay up too late.

17:11.500 --> 17:12.290
Okay.

17:13.420 --> 17:17.040
Helvetica isn't nearly maternal
 enough to be my mom.

17:17.040 --> 17:19.800
And how would you define "maternal"?

17:20.040 --> 17:21.440
An open heart!

17:21.440 --> 17:23.820
I want to feel enveloped by love.

17:23.820 --> 17:29.060
But that might not be what
 Mr. Bel is looking for.

17:29.780 --> 17:32.540
What kind of women do men like?

17:33.910 --> 17:36.580
How should we know?

17:36.900 --> 17:38.460
Women who are kind, maybe?

17:38.460 --> 17:43.070
No way! Most men aren't looking 
at what's on the inside.

17:43.300 --> 17:45.920
I-Isn't that a bit extreme?

17:46.190 --> 17:49.930
Hardly. The first thing 
men look at are a woman's breasts.

17:49.930 --> 17:52.700
Then her legs, then her face.

17:52.700 --> 17:56.230
Can't you feel them staring 
when you're dressed lightly?

17:57.090 --> 18:01.480
I see. I do think I know what 
you're talking about.

18:01.480 --> 18:04.590
Right? Especially when
 it comes to your chest...

18:07.880 --> 18:09.990
Why did you go quiet 
when you looked at me?

18:11.150 --> 18:13.370
I'm sorry, Ange.

18:13.370 --> 18:14.790
Why are you apologizing?

18:15.980 --> 18:19.270
Well, whatever. 
You're just saying boobs matter, right?

18:19.510 --> 18:23.370
You bet. Large breasts are 
definitely maternal material.

18:23.370 --> 18:26.030
Most men can't resist.

18:31.790 --> 18:35.170
Doesn't that make you 
quite motherly, Ms. Miri?

18:35.990 --> 18:37.010
No, not at all.

18:37.010 --> 18:37.950
Not one bit.

18:40.430 --> 18:43.670
That's totally unrelated!

18:45.380 --> 18:46.430
Jeez!

18:56.310 --> 18:58.610
I'm still stiff.

18:58.610 --> 18:59.880
Impressive.

19:00.460 --> 19:05.600
Your form and the precision of your blade 
make it hard to believe you have a peg leg.

19:05.600 --> 19:06.950
Thank you.

19:07.240 --> 19:10.970
But you still don't merit Lady Sasha's praise.

19:11.250 --> 19:14.970
Yes, I have to say I agree.

19:16.210 --> 19:19.380
I hear you're a swordsman as well.

19:19.380 --> 19:25.720
I am. I'm not as good as Lady Sasha, 
but I can wield a blade better than you.

19:26.330 --> 19:30.500
<i>I can see why he's upset that his mistress 
is fawning over a stranger</i>

19:30.500 --> 19:32.720
<i>who suddenly appeared out of nowhere.</i>

19:32.720 --> 19:38.000
<i>But he's honestly trying to evaluate my 
skill rather than being swayed by rumors.</i>

19:38.270 --> 19:44.370
I see. Lady Helvetica must feel safe 
with someone like you by her side.

19:44.620 --> 19:45.850
Don't flatter me.

19:46.420 --> 19:48.700
I don't care if you're the Red Ogre or not.

19:48.700 --> 19:50.860
Don't get ahead of yourself.

19:50.860 --> 19:54.140
I wouldn't dream of it.
I appreciate the warning.

19:54.140 --> 19:56.150
Good morning, Master.

19:56.930 --> 19:59.730
If you're willing, I'd like to duel.

19:59.730 --> 20:01.000
That's fine.

20:01.270 --> 20:04.680
I'll make you go all out against me today!

20:04.680 --> 20:06.210
Pardon me, my lady.

20:06.760 --> 20:10.410
But I don't believe this man is as 
good a swordsman as you say.

20:11.130 --> 20:12.550
What?

20:12.550 --> 20:15.880
I'm having trouble believing 
you lost to him.

20:15.880 --> 20:17.410
He must have played dirty.

20:17.410 --> 20:20.910
Silence! Try beating me 
before you talk like that.

20:20.910 --> 20:23.420
I couldn't beat you, Lady Sasha.

20:23.700 --> 20:26.920
But I wouldn't lose to him.

20:27.680 --> 20:30.550
How dare you insult my instructor?!

20:30.860 --> 20:31.960
Master!

20:32.750 --> 20:33.680
Yes?

20:33.680 --> 20:37.780
Please trounce this fool 
so he sees the truth.

20:38.220 --> 20:39.300
What?

20:40.330 --> 20:44.920
Very well. I shall wake 
you from your delusions.

20:45.770 --> 20:47.140
Come, Red Ogre.

20:47.140 --> 20:49.320
I shall defeat you soundly.

20:49.990 --> 20:52.310
Uh, okay...

20:55.860 --> 20:59.060
I've heard rumors of the 
Demon King slayer, too.

20:59.370 --> 21:01.600
You should delay your plans.

21:01.600 --> 21:06.080
It'd be reckless to antagonize both 
the Bordeaux family and her, milord.

21:07.300 --> 21:10.830
Sounds like Solomon wasn't 
very powerful after all.

21:11.190 --> 21:13.880
If you screw up, your head will roll.

21:13.880 --> 21:15.140
Be patient.

21:15.140 --> 21:17.830
I'm heading to Bordeaux after this.

21:18.180 --> 21:20.840
Hey, I just told you to delay your plans.

21:21.700 --> 21:23.730
Delay them to what end?

21:25.520 --> 21:31.110
I've endured years in this 
backwater waiting for this day.

21:31.110 --> 21:35.000
The powerful late Count Bordeaux is no more.

21:35.000 --> 21:37.830
His daughters may be talented,

21:37.830 --> 21:42.600
but compared to the wicked nobles 
in the capital, they're nothing.

21:42.990 --> 21:46.110
Nobles are different from the common rabble.

21:46.110 --> 21:48.750
And those girls ingratiate themselves

21:48.750 --> 21:51.380
by frolicking with commoners 
and cultivating the land.

21:51.670 --> 21:54.380
You listen to me. 
We'll act tonight, just as planned.

21:54.950 --> 21:56.930
Wealth and power...

21:56.930 --> 22:01.370
You understand that much, 
don't you, Saint of Solomon?

23:35.140 --> 23:40.050
<b>Next Time</b>

23:35.140 --> 23:40.050
<b>"Rebels Acting in Secret"</b>
